  #set text(size: 12pt)
  Results and Comparisons
]

#heading(depth: 2)[
  #set text(size: 11pt)
  MSE and PSNR Comparison
]

#p(2)[
  To compare with the results shown in test error MSE and PSNR metrics, using linear scaling actually provided an increase of approximately 3 dB in PSNR and a decrease of approximately 0.02 in MSE. Here are graphs showcasing the clamped and linear scaling metrics:

